<title>RUSSIA: Russian dockers paid in pineapples.</title>
<headline>Russian dockers paid in pineapples.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pineapples are cheaper than potatoes in the southern Russian port of Taganrog at the moment because dockers have been paid with tins of the exotic fruit rather than in roubles, Itar-Tass news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said the dockers were selling the tins on the streets to raise cash to buy food for their families.</p>
<p>Many Russian workers have not been paid for months, and cash-starved enterprises hand out all kinds of products from fish to saucepans in lieu of money.</p>
<p>The Kremlin has decreed that all public sector workers should receive wage arrears by the end of the year. Private enterprises are not covered by the announcement.</p>
